@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: what must be green before publishing images, and where each part runs
' covers: mise.toml
' covers: e2e/ladder_test.go
' covers: internal/contract/base_template_test.go
' Lineage and tags: image-lineage-and-publish.puml (same directory).
' Why the split exists: _spec/_experiments/nested-sbx-kvm.puml — sbx is host-only.
' Notes here are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── THE GATE IS IN TWO HALVES, AND THAT IS NOT A CHOICE ─────────────────────
' A proveo sandbox has docker but NOT sbx: the CLI is in no proveo image, and
' /dev/kvm does not exist there with no kvm module loaded. So the sbx-backed
' checks cannot run where the rest of them do, and a release gate that lives
' only in one place would either skip them or refuse to run at all.
'
' IN-SANDBOX (or any host with docker):
'   1  go build ./... && go vet ./... && go vet -tags e2e ./e2e/
'   2  go test ./...                     unit + contract
'   3  mise run build all                every image from source
'   4  mise run test-images              11 suites across all four defs
'   5  go test -tags e2e ./e2e/          the non-sbx e2e suite
'
' ON THE HOST ONLY, because each needs sbx:
'   6  the ladder, PER DEF — one climb per target, not one climb:
'        for t in cecli claudecode cursor opencode; do
'          PROVEO_LADDER_TEST=1 PROVEO_LADDER_TARGET=$t \
'            go test -tags e2e ./e2e/ -run Ladder -v
'        done
'      claudecode is the DEFAULT target, so a bare run measures only it. The
'      sbx fixes this suite proved for claudecode were applied to cursor by
'      SYMMETRY rather than measurement — a contract with one data point.
'   7  the credential control:
'        PROVEO_SBX_AGENT_KIT=1 PROVEO_LADDER_TEST=1 \
'        PROVEO_LADDER_TARGET=cecli go test -tags e2e ./e2e/ \
'          -run ProxyManagesTheCredential -v
'      It runs the SAME Kit twice, with and without credentials[], and fails if
'      both give the same value — so it proves the declaration CAUSES the
'      sentinel rather than merely coinciding with it.
'
' ── THE VERDICT ITSELF IS A THING THAT CAN BE WRONG ─────────────────────────
' `ladder-all` reads the ladder's result out of `go test` output, and it has
' misread it twice, in OPPOSITE directions:
'
'   1  a SKIP exits 0, so an unchecked exit status reported PASS for four defs
'      on a host with no sbx — four climbs that never happened, certified.
'   2  the fix grepped for "--- SKIP: TestSandboxLadder" UNANCHORED, which also
'      matches the four-space-indented SUBTEST line. cecli passed every rung
'      with only its browser rung skipped (there is no cecli-browser image) and
'      was reported as not-run.
'
' Go prints the top-level result flush left and indents subtests, so the anchor
' is the whole correctness of the line. The pattern is pinned by a contract
' test as `'^--- SKIP: TestSandboxLadder [(]'`, against the two shapes verbatim
' from real runs:
'
'   ran, one rung skipped   --- PASS: TestSandboxLadder (168.93s)
'                               --- SKIP: TestSandboxLadder/2-proveo-browser-image (0.14s)
'   never ran                   ladder_test.go:314: sbx not available: sbx not on PATH
'                           --- SKIP: TestSandboxLadder (0.00s)
'
' ── WHAT A GREEN GATE DOES NOT COVER ────────────────────────────────────────
' Stated because a checklist read as complete is worse than one read as partial:
'
'   amd64.  Every measurement in this branch is arm64. `deploy` pushes
'     amd64+arm64, so the publish is the first amd64 compile. The node tarball
'     picks per-arch with a pinned sha256 for each and the purge is dpkg, so it
'     is arch-independent BY INSPECTION — which is not a build.
'
'   the first-run consent prompt. With PROVEO_SBX_AGENT_KIT defaulted on, sbx
'     asks before injecting a service the operator has not yet bound — once per
'     service, recorded in ~/.config/sbx/credentials.yaml, and it asks even for
'     a credential it already holds. An UNATTENDED agent stops there. No test
'     covers it because it is interactive by definition.
'
'   TestProjectDotEnvAtEgressLayer/opencode is RED and unexplained. It runs a
'     stock ubuntu:24.04 image on the docker backend, so neither the base
'     rebase nor the agent-kit default can reach it.
'
' ── LEAKED STATE POISONS THE RESULT, AND HID FOR HOURS ──────────────────────
' Two proveo/opencode:local containers ran for SIX HOURS after the sessions
' that started them were killed, each holding a *-mitm-net network. They were
' invisible to `docker ps -a | grep proveo` because docker had named them
' `romantic_haibt` and `tender_rhodes` — proveo starts them without --name, so
' MATCH ON THE IMAGE, NEVER THE NAME:
'     docker ps -a --filter ancestor=proveo/opencode:local
' Removing them changed the dotenv failure from a 5m timeout to "session exited
' before a new -egress container", which is a different and more useful fault.
' The underlying defect is a teardown that does not run when a session is
' killed; cmd/proveo/clean.go exists for it and nothing invoked it.
' ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

title Release gate — two halves, because sbx is host-only

node "in-sandbox · docker only" as BOX <<host>> {
  component "build + vet + go test" as GO <<app>>
  component "build all\n14 images from source" as BUILD <<app>>
  component "test-images\n11 suites · 4 defs" as TI <<app>>
  component "e2e minus sbx" as E2E <<app>>
}

node "host only · needs sbx" as HOST <<host>> {
  component "ladder × 4 defs\ncecli claudecode cursor opencode" as LAD <<db>>
  component "credential control\nsame Kit, with and without" as CRED <<db>>
}

component "deploy all\namd64 + arm64 --push" as PUB <<cloud>>
component "not covered\namd64 · consent prompt · dotenv" as GAP <<error>>

GO ARROW_MAIN BUILD
BUILD ARROW_MAIN TI
TI ARROW_MAIN E2E
E2E ARROW_MAIN LAD : hand off to the host
LAD ARROW_MAIN CRED
CRED ARROW_MAIN PUB : only now
GAP ARROW_ERROR PUB : known blind spots

note bottom of LAD
  **One climb per def, not one climb.** The
  target defaults to claudecode, so a bare run
  measures a quarter of the fleet — and cursor
  inherited its fixes by symmetry rather than
  measurement.
end note

note bottom of LAD
  **A skip exits 0, so the verdict is grepped.**
  Unanchored it matched the indented SUBTEST line
  and called a full climb not-run; unchecked it
  called four absent climbs a pass. The pattern is
  anchored at column 0 and pinned by a test.
end note

note bottom of GAP
  **A checklist read as complete is worse than
  one read as partial.** amd64 has never been
  compiled here, the consent prompt is
  interactive by definition, and one e2e test
  is red for reasons still unknown.
end note

note bottom of TI
  **It prefers :local and PULLS otherwise.** A
  suite run without building first tested a
  seven-day-old published image and reported
  success — build all comes first for that
  reason, not for tidiness.
end note

note bottom of CRED
  **It proves causation, not coincidence.** The
  same Kit runs twice, with the credentials
  block and without, and an identical result
  either way fails the test.
end note

@enduml
